Assignment 3 - Customer Management Table

This is a retrospective learning/review version of the archived work.
The original code is retained in ../old with WRONG: comments.
Corrections and regression tests were prepared with OpenAI Codex assistance.
New explanatory comments start with CORRECTED:.

Build and run: ./run.sh
Regression checks: ./run.sh --test
The historical course sample binaries/test clients were not supplied.
No signed ethics document has been created or represented as the author's.

The array implementation grows in 1024-record units and has linear search.
It is simple and compact but scans empty slots and existing records.
The hash implementation owns each node once, indexes it by both ID/name,
and rehashes at 75% load by doubling buckets up to 2^20. Lookups are
expected O(1), with more pointer/storage overhead and O(n) rehash steps.
ExpandCustomerDB implements expansion; RegisterCustomer triggers it.
